       test evidence: unsupported  [tier: static]
         (no mapped test)
         recommended test: After adding a test to a file that already contains a mapped test, a criterion whose mapped tests were not edited keeps the same rating.
           inputs:  Use a prior review where the criterion already has a mapped test set containing at least one test, and a fresh run where that mapped test’s source is byte-identical but an additional, unrelated test is appended to the same test file. The criterion under test must not gain, lose, or edit any of its mapped tests; only the file containing them changes by addition of an unmapped test.
           detects: The implementation still treats any change to a file containing a mapped test as evidence that the criterion’s rating is stale, so appending an unrelated test to that file incorrectly causes the rating to change or be re-judged.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion adding-test-to-unmapped-file-leaves-rating-unchanged

